       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 3000 mg three times daily comes to 9,000 mg/day, which is more than twice the usual maximum of 4,000 mg/day for adults. Many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. A dose like this risks serious liver injury, even in a patient with normal liver function.\n\nHere are some common options. Please check them against your attending's plan and your hospital's protocol:\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily:** 3,000 mg/day.\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours:** 2,600 mg/day.\n- **1,000 mg PO every 8 hours:** 3,000 mg/day.\n- **500 to 1,000 mg PO every 6 hours as needed:** no more than 4,000 mg/day.\n\nYou may have meant 300 mg, 500 mg, or 1,000 mg per dose, or 3,000 mg total per day. Tell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it. Please also confirm it with your supervising resident or attending."
